    {
      "run": 2,
      "steps": 4,
      "narrative": "Having entered a cramped galley filled with the salty remnants of countless voyages, I conducted a thorough inspection of the space. The area was small and poorly maintained, with salt permeating almost every surface and leaving an unwelcome residue. To the north, there existed a doorway, while a hatch in the floor to the south led downwards. Among the sparse and utilitarian furnishings was a kettle, which I closely examined. The kettle appeared to be made of tin and was noticeably dented on one side, suggesting a life of hard use. Feeling the item might hold some value, or simply out of curiosity, I decided to take the kettle with me by picking it up from the floor. Regrettably, our exploration was limited by time or scope, as no further actions such as descending through the hatch or traveling northwards were recorded. The record compiled therefore details the initial discovery of a salt-encrusted galley with a battered tin kettle and the decision to collect the kettle, while any subsequent exploration or discoveries remain undocumented in the current report.",
