    {
      "run": 3,
      "steps": 12,
      "narrative": "Upon entering, I first noticed the cramped galley filled with the tang of salt. The galley had a north-bound doorway and a hatch leading down to the south. There, on the floor, lay a kettle dented on one side. I attempted to examine the kettle more closely, but no new information presented itself. Noticing a doorway to the north, I opened it to explore further, discovering a store. Here, empty shelves exuded the scent of paraffin. A coil of rope lay stiff with salt on the floor; I took it upon myself to examine and then take the rope. With the rope in hand, I moved westward only to find that movement was obstructed. Returning to the store and then heading south back to the galley, I dropped the rope, deciding its weight was unnecessary. Finally, I found myself examining the kettle once more, confirming its dented state, before closing the doorway back to the store, concluding my exploration without uncovering further secrets or items of interest within this salty, seafaring environment.",
