    {
      "run": 4,
      "steps": 12,
      "narrative": "In the cramped galley, salty remnants clung to everything. Initially, the examination of the kettle and floor revealed nothing out of the ordinary. I attempted to open the floor hatch but was unsuccessful. Moving eastward was unfeasible, so instead, I chose to investigate the northward pathways. First, I went north from the galley to find a sparse store smelling faintly of paraffin. Here, I successfully took a coil of rope from the floor before proceeding north again into a workshop. In this workshop, I examined an oil can and determined it to be half full. After adding the oil can to my inventory, I navigated eastward to a glass-walled lamp room. Within this room, devoid of much movement, I discovered a logbook resting on the floor. Without further delay, I picked up the logbook, concluding my exploration. Some tasks such as opening the hatch or traveling east from the galley remained unaccomplished due to obstruction or environmental constraints.",
